        "id": "93dea9a13af808cef517e0a6dfeaeb3147173c35",
        "tree_id": "da5d5363483eac436eceb41cc454a1399497559f",
        "message": "Stop generateNativeSecrets failing on CI when .env is absent\n\n.env is gitignored, so it exists on developer machines but never on a runner.\nGradle 9 validates a missing inputs.file(...) target even when .optional() was\ncalled, so every release build died at configuration time with \"specifies file\n'.env' which doesn't exist\" -- the cause of the red build.yml runs on main, and\nunrelated to the updater.\n\nTrack the file's presence as a property and only declare it as an input when it\nis actually there. Up-to-date behaviour is unchanged: a developer editing .env\nstill re-runs the task, and a runner without one records a stable false.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-03T18:55:30Z",
